 "result_text": "I changed the Uylings variant of `partition_asymmetry` in `neurom/features/bifurcation.py` so it no longer fails on typical morphologies. I didn't run any tests or try it on a real morphology.\n\nYou were right: it counted all nodes in each child subtree, so a bifurcation whose children are both leaves gave `n + m = 2` and hit the error.\n\n- **Counting:** the Uylings variant now counts terminal tips (leaves) in each subtree instead of all nodes.\n- **Both children are leaves:** it returns `0.0`, since the bifurcation is perfectly symmetric. Before, this case raised `NeuroMError`.\n- **Formula:** otherwise it still computes `|n - m| / (n + m - 2)`.\n\nThe default (non-Uylings) variant behaves as before. The `NeuroMError` import is still used elsewhere in the file. I didn't update the docstring.",
